  "id": "COMPOUND:41664 - PROTEIN:710",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cytisine, N-formyl- may be involved in the regulation of ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 (ABCA1) through multiple indirect pathways. The target of Cytisine, N-formyl- is Cholesteryl ester transfer protein (CETP), which in turn is targeted by Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin. This compound further targets ABCA1, indicating a potential pathway where Cytisine, N-formyl- influences ABCA1 via CETP. Similarly, Cytisine, N-formyl- targets HCT-8, which is also targeted by a complex compound that ultimately affects ABCA1. Additionally, Cytisine, N-formyl- interacts with Myosin light chain kinase 3, which is targeted by (2R)-pentan-2-ol, which also affects ABCA1. These findings suggest that Cytisine, N-formyl- may act as a modulator of ABCA1 through various intermediaries, potentially influencing lipid metabolism and cellular transport processes. The evidence is consistent with a regulatory mechanism where Cytisine, N-formyl- could influence ABCA1 through multiple pathways, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
